# Code owners review changes to the parts of Kaydo where a mistake leaks
# families' data or hands out access. With the "Require review from Code
# Owners" rule on main, a pull request touching these paths needs one of them
# to approve it.
#
# Everything else has no owner on purpose: any maintainer can review it.
#
# One owner for now. Add the team here (e.g. @kaydo/security) once there is
# one — and note that a lone owner cannot approve their own pull requests, so
# that rule only makes sense with a second person in each line.

# Who may read and write what
/firestore.rules                @Gnadi
/firestore.indexes.json         @Gnadi

# Viewer login, admin claims, the public mirror, push
/functions/                     @Gnadi

# Upload signing
/api/                           @Gnadi

# Client-side encryption
/src/utils/encryption.js        @Gnadi
/src/utils/encryptedUpload.js   @Gnadi
/src/context/AuthContext.jsx    @Gnadi

# CI, deploys, and who owns what
/.github/                       @Gnadi
/firebase.json                  @Gnadi
/vercel.json                    @Gnadi

# Security policy
/SECURITY.md                    @Gnadi
